### 5.2 WEB-Server (VLAN 20, HTTPS)

```bash
sudo hostnamectl set-hostname 20252241-WEB
sudo nano /etc/netplan/01-net.yaml
```
```yaml
network:
  version: 2
  ethernets:
    ens4:
      dhcp4: false
      addresses: [20.25.224.130/28]
      routes:
        - to: default
          via: 20.25.224.129
      nameservers:
        addresses: [8.8.8.8]
```
```bash
sudo chmod 600 /etc/netplan/01-net.yaml
sudo netplan apply

sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y apache2 php libapache2-mod-php php-mysql openssl
sudo a2enmod ssl
sudo openssl req -x509 -nodes -days 365 -newkey rsa:2048 \
  -keyout /etc/ssl/private/web.key -out /etc/ssl/certs/web.crt \
  -subj "/C=DO/O=Practica/CN=20.25.224.130"
sudo sed -i 's#/etc/ssl/certs/ssl-cert-snakeoil.pem#/etc/ssl/certs/web.crt#; s#/etc/ssl/private/ssl-cert-snakeoil.key#/etc/ssl/private/web.key#' /etc/apache2/sites-available/default-ssl.conf
sudo a2ensite default-ssl
sudo rm -f /var/www/html/index.html
sudo dd if=/dev/zero of=/var/www/html/prueba.exe bs=1k count=10
```

`/var/www/html/index.php` (página intencionalmente vulnerable a SQLi
para la demostración):
```php
<?php
mysqli_report(MYSQLI_REPORT_OFF);
$c = new mysqli("20.25.224.146","webuser","Web12345!","shop");
if ($c->connect_error) { die("Error DB: ".$c->connect_error); }
$id = $_GET['id'] ?? '1';
$r = $c->query("SELECT id,name FROM products WHERE id=$id");
echo "<h1>Tienda Demo</h1>";
if ($r) { while ($f = $r->fetch_assoc()) { echo $f['id']." - ".$f['name']."<br>"; } }
else { echo "Error: ".$c->error; }
?>
```
